PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":12322,"endIndex":12323,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12322,"endIndex":12323,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":12323,"endIndex":12450,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12323,"endIndex":12384,"textRun":{"content":"Examples: Illustrating Verification is Easier Than Generation","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":12384,"endIndex":12450,"textRun":{"content":". This is a very general property that holds across many domains:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":12450,"endIndex":12451,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12450,"endIndex":12451,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":12451,"endIndex":12721,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12451,"endIndex":12550,"textRun":{"content":"Formal Problems: In computational complexity theory, most computer scientists believe that P ≠ NP (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":12550,"endIndex":12559,"textRun":{"content":"Wikipedia","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P_versus_NP_problem#Reasons_to_believe_P_%E2%89%A0_NP_or_P_=_NP"}}}},{"startIndex":12559,"endIndex":12721,"textRun":{"content":"), which means there are many problems where checking a solution is easier than finding one. This is seen in tasks like solving SAT problems or graph algorithms.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.149phfcdx6cw","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":12721,"endIndex":12840,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12721,"endIndex":12840,"textRun":{"content":"Sports and Games: It's easier to look at a football scoreboard to see who is winning than it is to play the game well.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.149phfcdx6cw","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":12840,"endIndex":12975,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12840,"endIndex":12975,"textRun":{"content":"Consumer Products: Comparing the quality of smartphones based on user reviews is simpler than designing and building a new smartphone.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.149phfcdx6cw","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":12975,"endIndex":13080,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":12975,"endIndex":13080,"textRun":{"content":"Job Performance: Evaluating how well an employee is doing is less demanding than actually doing the job.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.149phfcdx6cw","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":13080,"endIndex":13189,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":13080,"endIndex":13189,"textRun":{"content":"Academic Research: While reviewing research can be tough, it's still less work than producing  new research.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.149phfcdx6cw","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":13189,"endIndex":13190,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":13189,"endIndex":13190,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":13190,"endIndex":13968,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":13190,"endIndex":13266,"textRun":{"content":"Why Verification Being Easier Than Generation Matters for Scalable Oversight","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":13266,"endIndex":13968,"textRun":{"content":". This fact is crucial for scalable oversight because it allows us as human overseers to efficiently ensure the correctness and safety of outputs produced by complex systems without needing to fully understand or replicate the entire generation process. If P ≠ NP is true , it implies that we might be able to trust and delegate alignment research itself to AI models, because we can comparatively easily verify that their solutions work while they have to do the hard task of generating the solutions to alignment. Overall operating under this assumption can make the task of aligning advanced AI systems seem more feasible. The next few paragraphs go into the debate of how valid this assumption is.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":13968,"endIndex":13969,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":13968,"endIndex":13969,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":13969,"endIndex":14785,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":13969,"endIndex":14005,"textRun":{"content":"Verification in Adversarial Contexts","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":14005,"endIndex":14785,"textRun":{"content":". When verifying something in situations where someone might be actively trying to trick or attack you, the process becomes much harder. Put another way, if we have AIs that are deceptive, the problem becomes significantly trickier. For example, making sure software is secure against all possible attacks can be tougher than writing the software in the first place. An attacker only needs to find one security hole, but the person verifying must check everything to ensure there are no holes. This makes verification very challenging. Similarly creating a secure system in cryptography is hard, but proving that it’s secure against all possible attacks is even more difficult. You need to consider every potential way someone might try to break the system, which is a huge task.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":14785,"endIndex":14786,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":14785,"endIndex":14786,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":14786,"endIndex":15487,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":14786,"endIndex":14846,"textRun":{"content":"Easier than generation does not mean verification is trivial","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":14846,"endIndex":15487,"textRun":{"content":". Just because verification is theoretically easier than generation doesn’t mean it’s always easy in practice. For example, checking a complex mathematical proof can be very hard. Writing the proof takes creativity and deep understanding, but verifying it requires careful and detailed checking, which can be exhausting and prone to mistakes. In the case of software, writing secure software is challenging, but verifying that it’s completely secure is even harder. Even though verifying a problem’s solution might be easier than generating the solution, the process can still be very difficult and require significant effort and expertise.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":15487,"endIndex":15488,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":15487,"endIndex":15488,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":15488,"endIndex":16085,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":15488,"endIndex":15533,"textRun":{"content":"Verification of Safety vs. Provable Alignment","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":15533,"endIndex":16085,"textRun":{"content":". In the event that we have to deal with superintelligent AI, just verifying its behavior might not be enough. Some researchers argue that we need to prove that the AI will always act in ways that align with human values. Verification means checking whether the AI behaves correctly in specific situations. Provable alignment means giving solid evidence that the AI will act correctly in every possible situation, even new and unexpected ones. This requires more than just checking—it needs formal methods and guarantees, which is extremely difficult.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":16085,"endIndex":16086,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16085,"endIndex":16086,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":16086,"endIndex":16546,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16086,"endIndex":16121,"textRun":{"content":"Verification vs. Mathematical Proof","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":16121,"endIndex":16546,"textRun":{"content":". Verification involves checking if a specific solution is correct, usually through testing or inspection. A mathematical proof, on the other hand, is a rigorous logical argument that shows a statement is always true. For example, verifying a Sudoku solution checks if the given arrangement is correct, while a mathematical proof might show that any Sudoku puzzle with a certain number of clues always has a unique solution.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":16546,"endIndex":16547,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16546,"endIndex":16547,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":16547,"endIndex":16566,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16547,"endIndex":16566,"textRun":{"content":"Task Decomposition\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":26,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Book Antiqua","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"headingId":"h.2ofwjll5qh58","namedStyleType":"HEADING_1","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":16566,"endIndex":16567,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16566,"endIndex":16567,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":16567,"endIndex":16720,"table":{"rows":2,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":16568,"endIndex":16596,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":16569,"endIndex":16575,"content":[{"startIndex":16570,"endIndex":16575,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16570,"endIndex":16575,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":16575,"endIndex":16596,"content":[{"startIndex":16576,"endIndex":16596,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16576,"endIndex":16596,"textRun":{"content":"section-description\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":16596,"endIndex":16719,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":16597,"endIndex":16606,"content":[{"startIndex":16598,"endIndex":16606,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16598,"endIndex":16606,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":16606,"endIndex":16719,"content":[{"startIndex":16607,"endIndex":16719,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16607,"endIndex":16719,"textRun":{"content":"To make scaling oversight manageable, we can break down large, complex tasks into smaller, verifiable subtasks.\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":16720,"endIndex":16721,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16720,"endIndex":16721,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":16721,"endIndex":17199,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":16721,"endIndex":16748,"textRun":{"content":"What is Task Decomposition?","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":16748,"endIndex":17199,"textRun":{"content":" Task decomposition is the process of breaking down a complex task into smaller, more manageable subtasks. This technique makes it easier to tackle sophisticated problems by dividing them into simpler components that can be addressed independently. For example, if you need to summarize a book, you could break down this larger task into summarizing each chapter individually. Each chapter summary then contributes to the overall summary of the book.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":17199,"endIndex":17208,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17199,"endIndex":17208,"textRun":{"content":"Example:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":17208,"endIndex":17234,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17208,"endIndex":17234,"textRun":{"content":"Task: Summarize the book.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.a08myqluhjer","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":17234,"endIndex":17284,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17234,"endIndex":17284,"textRun":{"content":"Decomposition: Summarize each chapter separately.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.a08myqluhjer","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":17284,"endIndex":17285,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17284,"endIndex":17285,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":17285,"endIndex":17771,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17285,"endIndex":17771,"textRun":{"content":"Decomposing tasks can be thought of as a method of overcoming complexity. Humans navigate the world's complexity by using layers of abstraction, where each layer hides most of the underlying details, allowing us to focus on manageable chunks of information. This ability is important because humans can only keep track of a few pieces of information in their mind simultaneously. Task decomposition helps us solve highly complex problems by breaking them down into simpler subproblems.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":17771,"endIndex":17772,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17771,"endIndex":17772,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":17772,"endIndex":18271,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":17772,"endIndex":17809,"textRun":{"content":"What is Recursive Task Decomposition?","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":17809,"endIndex":18271,"textRun":{"content":" Recursive task decomposition extends the basic concept by breaking down each sub-task into even more granular subtasks. This iterative process continues until each task is simple enough to solve directly. Continuing with the book summarization example, recursive task decomposition would involve further breaking down each chapter summary into page summaries, and each page summary into paragraph summaries until the task is simple enough to evaluate directly.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":18271,"endIndex":18280,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18271,"endIndex":18280,"textRun":{"content":"Example:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":18280,"endIndex":18306,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18280,"endIndex":18306,"textRun":{"content":"Task: Summarize the book.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.9z5dloo7iab5","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":18306,"endIndex":18321,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18306,"endIndex":18321,"textRun":{"content":"Decomposition:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.9z5dloo7iab5","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":18321,"endIndex":18345,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18321,"endIndex":18345,"textRun":{"content":"Summarize each chapter.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":54,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":72,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.9z5dloo7iab5","nestingLevel":1,"textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":18345,"endIndex":18386,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18345,"endIndex":18386,"textRun":{"content":"Summarize each page within each chapter.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":54,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":72,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.9z5dloo7iab5","nestingLevel":1,"textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":18386,"endIndex":18429,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18386,"endIndex":18429,"textRun":{"content":"Summarize each paragraph within each page.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":54,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":72,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.9z5dloo7iab5","nestingLevel":1,"textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":18429,"endIndex":18430,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18429,"endIndex":18430,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":18430,"endIndex":19226,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":18431,"endIndex":18446,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":18432,"endIndex":18438,"content":[{"startIndex":18433,"endIndex":18438,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18433,"endIndex":18438,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":18438,"endIndex":18446,"content":[{"startIndex":18439,"endIndex":18446,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18439,"endIndex":18446,"textRun":{"content":"figure\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":18446,"endIndex":18460,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":18447,"endIndex":18456,"content":[{"startIndex":18448,"endIndex":18456,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18448,"endIndex":18456,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":18456,"endIndex":18460,"content":[{"startIndex":18457,"endIndex":18458,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18457,"endIndex":18458,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}},{"startIndex":18458,"endIndex":18460,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18458,"endIndex":18459,"inlineObjectElement":{"inlineObjectId":"kix.qyr5qvz97moe","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":18459,"endIndex":18460,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":18460,"endIndex":19225,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":18461,"endIndex":18470,"content":[{"startIndex":18462,"endIndex":18470,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18462,"endIndex":18470,"textRun":{"content":"caption\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":18470,"endIndex":19225,"content":[{"startIndex":18471,"endIndex":19225,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":18471,"endIndex":19208,"textRun":{"content":"Example of summarizing books that combines task decomposition with learning from human feedback. The book is first decomposed into multiple chunks using a fixed (not learned) chunking algorithm (height 0). Then humans provide demonstrations summarizing these chunks, which is used to train an ML model on this data using behavior cloning. Then more data is collected from humans who compare different model outputs which is then used to further train a summarization policy using reward modeling. Then summaries are concatenated (height 0), data is collected for summarizing these summaries, and the model is fine-tuned for this summarization task (height 1). This procedure is repeated recursively until the entire book is summarized. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":19208,"endIndex":19223,"textRun":{"content":"Wu et al., 2021","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.10862"}}}},{"startIndex":19223,"endIndex":19225,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":19226,"endIndex":19227,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":19226,"endIndex":19227,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":19227,"endIndex":19892,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":19227,"endIndex":19293,"textRun":{"content":"How does task decomposition help generate better training signals?","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":19293,"endIndex":19892,"textRun":{"content":" As we mentioned in the earlier sections, when AI systems become more capable, it becomes difficult for humans to provide the right training signals or data, especially for tasks that have subjective evaluation criteria (fuzzy tasks). The core thing that we are trying to do with task decomposition is to reduce the difficulty of providing a training signal to human judgment. Simpler tasks, means that it is easier to provide a training signal, it also means that the tasks are easier to verify. Therefore task decomposition is quite important to the success of many scalable oversight techniques.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":19892,"endIndex":19893,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":19892,"endIndex":19893,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":19893,"endIndex":20160,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":19893,"endIndex":20160,"textRun":{"content":"Decomposing a task involves breaking it down into smaller, more manageable parts. These parts help you understand and manage the task better, but they may not always be independently solvable or reusable. The key properties we want from a good decomposition include:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":20160,"endIndex":20161,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":20160,"endIndex":20161,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":20161,"endIndex":20460,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":20161,"endIndex":20460,"textRun":{"content":"Recursive Decomposability: The system should be capable of recursive task decomposition, thereby dividing a problem into simpler sub-tasks. For example, summarizing a book involves breaking it down into chapters, then pages, and then paragraphs until we reach some minimum level of task difficulty.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.2lfpr12p1per","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":20460,"endIndex":20716,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":20460,"endIndex":20716,"textRun":{"content":"Independence/Modularity: Individual sub-tasks should be able to be completed independently and in parallel without relying on each other or the overall task. For example, each summarizer focuses on a paragraph without needing to understand the whole book.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.2lfpr12p1per","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":20716,"endIndex":20995,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":20716,"endIndex":20995,"textRun":{"content":"Composability: We should be able to combine the solutions of individual independent sub-tasks into a coherent and comprehensive solution to the original problem. For example, combining all the independent chapter/paragraph summaries to get a complete summary of the entire book.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.2lfpr12p1per","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":20995,"endIndex":20996,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":20995,"endIndex":20996,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":20996,"endIndex":21702,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":20996,"endIndex":21039,"textRun":{"content":"Task Decomposition in the learning process.","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":21039,"endIndex":21702,"textRun":{"content":" When we break down a complicated task into smaller sub-tasks, each sub-task becomes simpler to understand and solve. This process allows learners to build their knowledge incrementally, focusing on one small piece at a time. As each piece is understood and mastered, the learner gradually constructs a comprehensive understanding of the larger task. Since this principle works well for humans, a natural question is whether we can use something similar in the machine learning process to provide better training signals to our models. This is what we explore in the next sections, trying to emulate the entire human cognitive process through factored cognition.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":21702,"endIndex":21703,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":21702,"endIndex":21703,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":21703,"endIndex":21722,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":21703,"endIndex":21722,"textRun":{"content":"Factored Cognition\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"headingId":"h.c7yohpcg261k","namedStyleType":"HEADING_2","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":21722,"endIndex":21723,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":21722,"endIndex":21723,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":21723,"endIndex":22046,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":21723,"endIndex":21750,"textRun":{"content":"What is Factored Cognition?","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":21750,"endIndex":22046,"textRun":{"content":" Factored cognition is a way to help machine learning (ML) models replicate human thinking (cognition) by breaking down complex cognitive tasks into smaller subtasks. It leverages this principle of overcoming complexity by decomposing a problem into smaller subproblems that are easier to solve.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":22046,"endIndex":22047,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22046,"endIndex":22047,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":22047,"endIndex":22543,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22047,"endIndex":22543,"textRun":{"content":"By imagining cognition itself as a fuzzy task, we can use task factorization to decompose thinking into a series of tasks and make it possible to train ML models with accurate training signals emulating human cognition. By recording how humans solve problems using explicit actions in narrow contexts, we can train ML systems to imitate these processes. These systems can then serve as trusted assistants, handling more tasks and augmenting human cognitive capacity for evaluation and oversight.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":22543,"endIndex":22544,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22543,"endIndex":22544,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":22544,"endIndex":22785,"table":{"rows":4,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":22545,"endIndex":22564,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":22546,"endIndex":22552,"content":[{"startIndex":22547,"endIndex":22552,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22547,"endIndex":22552,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{"bold":true,"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.9529412,"green":0.9529412,"blue":0.9529412}}},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":22552,"endIndex":22564,"content":[{"startIndex":22553,"endIndex":22564,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22553,"endIndex":22564,"textRun":{"content":"definition\n","textStyle":{"bold":true,"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.9529412,"green":0.9529412,"blue":0.9529412}}},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":22564,"endIndex":22591,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":22565,"endIndex":22571,"content":[{"startIndex":22566,"endIndex":22571,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22566,"endIndex":22571,"textRun":{"content":"term\n","textStyle":{"bold":true,"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":22571,"endIndex":22591,"content":[{"startIndex":22572,"endIndex":22591,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22572,"endIndex":22590,"textRun":{"content":"Factored Cognition","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":22590,"endIndex":22591,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":22591,"endIndex":22615,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":22592,"endIndex":22600,"content":[{"startIndex":22593,"endIndex":22600,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22593,"endIndex":22600,"textRun":{"content":"source\n","textStyle":{"bold":true,"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":22600,"endIndex":22615,"content":[{"startIndex":22601,"endIndex":22615,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22601,"endIndex":22602,"textRun":{"content":"(","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":22602,"endIndex":22613,"textRun":{"content":"Ought, 2018","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://ought.org/research/factored-cognition"}}}},{"startIndex":22613,"endIndex":22614,"textRun":{"content":")","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":22614,"endIndex":22615,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":22615,"endIndex":22784,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":22616,"endIndex":22625,"content":[{"startIndex":22617,"endIndex":22625,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22617,"endIndex":22625,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{"bold":true,"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":22625,"endIndex":22784,"content":[{"startIndex":22626,"endIndex":22784,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22626,"endIndex":22783,"textRun":{"content":"Factored cognition refers to mechanisms where sophisticated learning and reasoning is broken down (or factored) into many small and mostly independent tasks.","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":22783,"endIndex":22784,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":22785,"endIndex":22786,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22785,"endIndex":22786,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":22786,"endIndex":22787,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22786,"endIndex":22787,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":22787,"endIndex":22788,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22787,"endIndex":22788,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":22788,"endIndex":23144,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":22788,"endIndex":23144,"textRun":{"content":"Consider the cognitive task of deciding how to invest $100,000 to achieve the most social good. A human would need to analyze various factors, predict outcomes, and make informed decisions. By subdividing this task into smaller, more manageable subtasks, each of which can be solved using clear training signals, we can delegate these tasks to ML systems.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":23144,"endIndex":23145,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23144,"endIndex":23145,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":23145,"endIndex":23446,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":23146,"endIndex":23161,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":23147,"endIndex":23153,"content":[{"startIndex":23148,"endIndex":23153,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23148,"endIndex":23153,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":23153,"endIndex":23161,"content":[{"startIndex":23154,"endIndex":23161,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23154,"endIndex":23161,"textRun":{"content":"figure\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":23161,"endIndex":23175,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":23162,"endIndex":23171,"content":[{"startIndex":23163,"endIndex":23171,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23163,"endIndex":23171,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":23171,"endIndex":23175,"content":[{"startIndex":23172,"endIndex":23173,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23172,"endIndex":23173,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}},{"startIndex":23173,"endIndex":23175,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23173,"endIndex":23174,"inlineObjectElement":{"inlineObjectId":"kix.h86m09caitdf","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":23174,"endIndex":23175,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":23175,"endIndex":23445,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":23176,"endIndex":23185,"content":[{"startIndex":23177,"endIndex":23185,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23177,"endIndex":23185,"textRun":{"content":"caption\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":23185,"endIndex":23445,"content":[{"startIndex":23186,"endIndex":23445,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23186,"endIndex":23431,"textRun":{"content":"This figure illustrates the process of breaking down a complex research question concerning azithromycin into multiple sub-questions. The sub-questions are gradually simplified until they can be addressed through a single language model query. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":23431,"endIndex":23442,"textRun":{"content":"Ought, 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://primer.ought.org/"}}}},{"startIndex":23442,"endIndex":23445,"textRun":{"content":").\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":23446,"endIndex":23447,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23446,"endIndex":23447,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":23447,"endIndex":23489,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23447,"endIndex":23489,"textRun":{"content":"Key advantages of factored cognition are:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":23489,"endIndex":23490,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23489,"endIndex":23490,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":23490,"endIndex":24010,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":23490,"endIndex":23501,"textRun":{"content":"Delegation:","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":23501,"endIndex":24009,"textRun":{"content":" Since the tasks are factored, we can assign subtasks to different agents who can work on them independently. This involves providing clear instructions and expected outcomes for each agent. For example, different agents (summarizers) can be assigned specific chapters to summarize. These agents can further delegate the task of summarizing to sub-agents who focus on individual pages or paragraphs. Each agent works independently, focusing solely on their part without needing to understand the entire book.","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":24009,"endIndex":24010,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.2b5gt4mk2dn9","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":24010,"endIndex":24011,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":24010,"endIndex":24011,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":24011,"endIndex":24782,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":24011,"endIndex":24025,"textRun":{"content":"Meta-reasoning","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":24025,"endIndex":24782,"textRun":{"content":": Factored cognition also involves applying this thinking to the decomposition process itself. If tasks can be factored into independently solvable sub-tasks, then factoring itself can be thought of as a task that can be factored. This involves reasoning about the decomposition process, learning from previous attempts, adjusting strategies, and continually improving the decomposition to ensure each sub-task is self-contained and manageable. Initially, humans can perform meta-reasoning by overseeing the decomposition process, deciding how to break down complex tasks, and when to stop further decomposition. In advanced systems, sub-agents (AI models) can also perform meta-reasoning by learning from humans and applying these strategies autonomously.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.2b5gt4mk2dn9","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":24782,"endIndex":24783,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":24782,"endIndex":24783,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":24783,"endIndex":25047,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":24783,"endIndex":25047,"textRun":{"content":"This approach to decomposing problems mirrors human thought. When we think, we often alternate between decomposing and solving problems. By breaking down a problem into smaller parts and solving each part, we manage complexity and make the task more approachable.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":25047,"endIndex":25048,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25047,"endIndex":25048,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":25048,"endIndex":25302,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25048,"endIndex":25302,"textRun":{"content":"Factored cognition is a general approach that can be used in different ways. Later sections will explore iterated distillation and amplification (IDA) and debate both of which use task factoring as a tool in their larger alignment approach to AI Safety.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":25302,"endIndex":25303,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25302,"endIndex":25303,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}},{"startIndex":25303,"endIndex":25321,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25303,"endIndex":25320,"textRun":{"content":"Process Oversight","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":25320,"endIndex":25321,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true,"fontSize":{"magnitude":23,"unit":"PT"}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"headingId":"h.zduhuau7o2r3","namedStyleType":"HEADING_1","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":25321,"endIndex":25322,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25321,"endIndex":25322,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":25322,"endIndex":25570,"table":{"rows":2,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":25323,"endIndex":25351,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":25324,"endIndex":25330,"content":[{"startIndex":25325,"endIndex":25330,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25325,"endIndex":25330,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":25330,"endIndex":25351,"content":[{"startIndex":25331,"endIndex":25351,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25331,"endIndex":25351,"textRun":{"content":"section-description\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":25351,"endIndex":25569,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":25352,"endIndex":25361,"content":[{"startIndex":25353,"endIndex":25361,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25353,"endIndex":25361,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}}}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":25361,"endIndex":25569,"content":[{"startIndex":25362,"endIndex":25569,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25362,"endIndex":25569,"textRun":{"content":"Instead of only judging an AI's final answer, we can supervise an AI's reasoning steps, providing more precise feedback. This makes it harder for the AI to fake good results with clever but wrong reasoning.\n","textStyle":{"fontSize":{"magnitude":11,"unit":"PT"},"weightedFontFamily":{"fontFamily":"Merriweather","weight":400}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":25570,"endIndex":25571,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25570,"endIndex":25571,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":25571,"endIndex":25741,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25571,"endIndex":25741,"textRun":{"content":"Learning a new task can be approached via trial and error, known as outcome-oriented learning, where the agent's strategy is determined entirely by the desired outcome. \n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":25741,"endIndex":25742,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25741,"endIndex":25742,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":25742,"endIndex":26074,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":25742,"endIndex":26074,"textRun":{"content":"Machine learning over the last decades has been showing a trend toward outcome-based systems. Which is to say that models are trained end-to-end and only the final output of the AI is what we provide a training signal for. This is called outcome-based oversight, but there is an alternative approach called process-based oversight.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":26074,"endIndex":26075,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26074,"endIndex":26075,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":26075,"endIndex":26908,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26075,"endIndex":26107,"textRun":{"content":"What is process-based oversight?","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":26107,"endIndex":26908,"textRun":{"content":" The outcome based approach only oversees the final result of a model's process. It is primarily concerned with whether the final answer is correct, not how the answer was derived. As an example, a model tasked with solving a math problem would only be evaluated on whether it produced the correct solution, regardless of the steps it took to get there. Process-based oversight on the other hand currently relies on human-understandable task decompositions with direct supervision of intermediate steps. This approach supervises the reasoning process itself, including all intermediate steps. It ensures that each step leading to the final result is logical and correct. For example, in solving a math problem, every calculation and logical step taken by the model would be evaluated for correctness.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":26908,"endIndex":26909,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26908,"endIndex":26909,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":26909,"endIndex":27323,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":26910,"endIndex":26925,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":26911,"endIndex":26917,"content":[{"startIndex":26912,"endIndex":26917,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26912,"endIndex":26917,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":26917,"endIndex":26925,"content":[{"startIndex":26918,"endIndex":26925,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26918,"endIndex":26925,"textRun":{"content":"figure\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":26925,"endIndex":26939,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":26926,"endIndex":26935,"content":[{"startIndex":26927,"endIndex":26935,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26927,"endIndex":26935,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":26935,"endIndex":26939,"content":[{"startIndex":26936,"endIndex":26937,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26936,"endIndex":26937,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}},{"startIndex":26937,"endIndex":26939,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26937,"endIndex":26938,"inlineObjectElement":{"inlineObjectId":"kix.hjjc2bc0tzr0","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":26938,"endIndex":26939,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":26939,"endIndex":27322,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":26940,"endIndex":26949,"content":[{"startIndex":26941,"endIndex":26949,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26941,"endIndex":26949,"textRun":{"content":"caption\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":26949,"endIndex":27322,"content":[{"startIndex":26950,"endIndex":27322,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":26950,"endIndex":27192,"textRun":{"content":"Prerequisite to overseeing the reasoning, is actually getting the model to output its reasoning. One common example is CoT prompting. CoT enables large language models to tackle complex arithmetic, commonsense, and symbolic reasoning tasks. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":27192,"endIndex":27208,"textRun":{"content":"Wei et al., 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903"}}}},{"startIndex":27208,"endIndex":27299,"textRun":{"content":") But it also allows us to oversee the “thought process” in addition to the final answer. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":27299,"endIndex":27320,"textRun":{"content":"Lightman et. al, 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20050"}}}},{"startIndex":27320,"endIndex":27322,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":27323,"endIndex":27324,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":27323,"endIndex":27324,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":27324,"endIndex":28260,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":27324,"endIndex":27374,"textRun":{"content":"Process supervision makes credit assignment easier","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":27374,"endIndex":28260,"textRun":{"content":". The credit assignment problem involves determining which specific actions or sequences of events were responsible for producing a particular outcome or reward. Think of a chess game where a player makes seemingly correct moves but ultimately loses. The credit assignment problem here involves identifying which specific moves led to the loss. Outcome based supervision would just say you won or you lost which makes it very difficult to determine which sequence of moves were actually very good even though you lost the game. Process supervision makes this easier by providing more precise feedback than outcome supervision.  Process supervision is similar to reward shaping, where small intermediate 'fake' rewards help the learning agent converge more quickly. This approach provides feedback on each intermediate step or trains models to imitate the human decision-making process.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":28260,"endIndex":28261,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28260,"endIndex":28261,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":28261,"endIndex":28576,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":28262,"endIndex":28277,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":28263,"endIndex":28269,"content":[{"startIndex":28264,"endIndex":28269,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28264,"endIndex":28269,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":28269,"endIndex":28277,"content":[{"startIndex":28270,"endIndex":28277,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28270,"endIndex":28277,"textRun":{"content":"figure\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":28277,"endIndex":28291,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":28278,"endIndex":28287,"content":[{"startIndex":28279,"endIndex":28287,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28279,"endIndex":28287,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":28287,"endIndex":28291,"content":[{"startIndex":28288,"endIndex":28289,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28288,"endIndex":28289,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}},{"startIndex":28289,"endIndex":28291,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28289,"endIndex":28290,"inlineObjectElement":{"inlineObjectId":"kix.rzitbbut2s0n","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":28290,"endIndex":28291,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":28291,"endIndex":28575,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":28292,"endIndex":28301,"content":[{"startIndex":28293,"endIndex":28301,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28293,"endIndex":28301,"textRun":{"content":"caption\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":28301,"endIndex":28575,"content":[{"startIndex":28302,"endIndex":28575,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28302,"endIndex":28552,"textRun":{"content":"An example of process oversight feedback. The image is a screenshot of the interface used to collect feedback for each step in a solution. This shows the correct reasoning process being followed and reinforced, even if the ultimate answer is wrong. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":28552,"endIndex":28573,"textRun":{"content":"Lightman et. al, 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20050"}}}},{"startIndex":28573,"endIndex":28575,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":28576,"endIndex":28577,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28576,"endIndex":28577,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":28577,"endIndex":29051,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":28577,"endIndex":28617,"textRun":{"content":"Safety implications of process oversight","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":28617,"endIndex":29027,"textRun":{"content":". Outcome based oversight might result in specification gaming. Process based supervision on the other hand theoretically mitigates this problem to a large extent by being more likely to produce correct and legible reasoning. It encourages models to follow a process endorsed by humans and directly rewards an aligned sequence of smaller steps rather than relying on outcomes as a proxy for aligned behavior. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":29027,"endIndex":29048,"textRun":{"content":"Lightman et. al, 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20050"}}}},{"startIndex":29048,"endIndex":29051,"textRun":{"content":") \n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":29051,"endIndex":29052,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":29051,"endIndex":29052,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":29052,"endIndex":29587,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":29052,"endIndex":29153,"textRun":{"content":"Generally, for fuzzy tasks, process based supervision might be a more appropriate method to pursue. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":29153,"endIndex":29172,"textRun":{"content":"Uesato et. al, 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.14275"}}}},{"startIndex":29172,"endIndex":29405,"textRun":{"content":") For example, when we need to verify the chain of mathematical reasoning, research so far has found that process supervision significantly outperforms outcome supervision for training models to solve problems for math based tasks. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":29405,"endIndex":29426,"textRun":{"content":"Lightman et. al, 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20050"}}}},{"startIndex":29426,"endIndex":29460,"textRun":{"content":") Process based supervision might ","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":29460,"endIndex":29469,"textRun":{"content":"similarly","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":29469,"endIndex":29587,"textRun":{"content":" result in more aligned outcomes for other complex chains of reasoning such as long term planning or decision making.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":29587,"endIndex":29588,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":29587,"endIndex":29588,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":29588,"endIndex":30420,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":29588,"endIndex":30117,"textRun":{"content":"One problem is that due to the higher feedback requirement at every step, process based methods require a greater degree of human expertise. As a concrete example, if we were training a model to generate new CPU designs, we can simply structure outcome-based feedback based on power-consumption, chip area, etc. These are easier to evaluate and give feedback on, and can be used to optimize the overall chip layouts. On the other hand, a process-based approach would require detailed expert knowledge on designing chip layouts. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":30117,"endIndex":30136,"textRun":{"content":"Uesato et. al, 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2211.14275"}}}},{"startIndex":30136,"endIndex":30420,"textRun":{"content":") So even though process based oversight methods might potentially lead to both higher capabilities and alignment outcomes, they rely on amplifying human overseer abilities. We will explore how to increase the capability of human overseers in the section on amplification and debate.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":30420,"endIndex":30421,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":30420,"endIndex":30421,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":30421,"endIndex":30557,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":30421,"endIndex":30557,"textRun":{"content":"The next couple of sections explore two methods of process based supervision - externalized reasoning oversight and procedural cloning.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":30557,"endIndex":30558,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":30557,"endIndex":30558,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":30558,"endIndex":30597,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":30558,"endIndex":30597,"textRun":{"content":"Externalized Reasoning Oversight (ERO)\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"headingId":"h.cmzevx3o131p","namedStyleType":"HEADING_2","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":30597,"endIndex":30598,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":30597,"endIndex":30598,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":30598,"endIndex":31362,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":30598,"endIndex":31186,"textRun":{"content":"Externalized reasoning oversight (ERO), sometimes referred to as verbalized reasoning, revolves around the idea of encouraging language models (LLMs) to \"think out loud.\" This approach aims to have models reveal their reasoning steps in natural language before they output an action or a decision. By decomposing complex reasoning into smaller steps and making it transparent, we can provide detailed training signals and oversight. This makes guiding the reasoning process of our models easier, and might potentially be more effective than only evaluating the final outputs or actions. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":31186,"endIndex":31197,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/FRRb6Gqem8k69ocbi/externalized-reasoning-oversight-a-research-direction-for"}}}},{"startIndex":31197,"endIndex":31362,"textRun":{"content":") This also can potentially serve as a complementary approach to the entire field of interpretability which can be thought of as “internalized reasoning oversight.”\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":31362,"endIndex":31363,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":31362,"endIndex":31363,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":31363,"endIndex":31946,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":31363,"endIndex":31469,"textRun":{"content":"Externalized reasoning can potentially prevent undesirable behaviors such as deception and power-seeking (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":31469,"endIndex":31480,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/FRRb6Gqem8k69ocbi/externalized-reasoning-oversight-a-research-direction-for"}}}},{"startIndex":31480,"endIndex":31946,"textRun":{"content":"), although this has yet to be empirically verified. The argument is that when a model's reasoning is visible, we can directly observe the logic it follows and identify any problematic thought patterns or chains of reasoning. This level of oversight is not possible when we only look at the final outputs of the model, as we miss the underlying reasoning that led to those outputs. To be able to rely on ERO, we need to make sure that the externalized reasoning is:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":31946,"endIndex":31947,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":31946,"endIndex":31947,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":31947,"endIndex":32061,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":31947,"endIndex":31967,"textRun":{"content":"Causally Responsible","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":31967,"endIndex":32061,"textRun":{"content":": The reasoning should directly lead to the conclusion without any post-hoc rationalizations.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.djj3pbd6mea0","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":32061,"endIndex":32167,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32061,"endIndex":32069,"textRun":{"content":"Complete","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":32069,"endIndex":32167,"textRun":{"content":": All necessary steps in the reasoning process should be present, with no critical steps omitted.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.djj3pbd6mea0","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":32167,"endIndex":32283,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32167,"endIndex":32182,"textRun":{"content":"Straightforward","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":32182,"endIndex":32283,"textRun":{"content":": The reasoning should be clear and free from hidden messages or deceptive encoding (steganography).\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.djj3pbd6mea0","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":32283,"endIndex":32284,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32283,"endIndex":32284,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":32284,"endIndex":32933,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32284,"endIndex":32326,"textRun":{"content":"How is ERO related to task decomposition? ","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":32326,"endIndex":32451,"textRun":{"content":"Chain-of-Thought (CoT) decomposition is the primary way that researchers currently approach externalized reasoning oversight.","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":32451,"endIndex":32452,"textRun":{"content":" ","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":32452,"endIndex":32786,"textRun":{"content":"Task decomposition involves breaking down a complex task into simpler subtasks, each of which can be handled independently. Chain-of-thought decomposition is a technique within the broader framework of task decomposition, specifically focused on both enhancing and allowing externalized oversight of the reasoning processes in LLMs. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":32786,"endIndex":32802,"textRun":{"content":"Wei et. al; 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903"}}}},{"startIndex":32802,"endIndex":32933,"textRun":{"content":") For the rest of this section when we talk about externalized reasoning oversight we are referring to chain-of-thought reasoning.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":32933,"endIndex":32934,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32933,"endIndex":32934,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":32934,"endIndex":33483,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":32935,"endIndex":32950,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":32936,"endIndex":32942,"content":[{"startIndex":32937,"endIndex":32942,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32937,"endIndex":32942,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":32942,"endIndex":32950,"content":[{"startIndex":32943,"endIndex":32950,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32943,"endIndex":32950,"textRun":{"content":"figure\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":32950,"endIndex":32964,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":32951,"endIndex":32960,"content":[{"startIndex":32952,"endIndex":32960,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32952,"endIndex":32960,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":32960,"endIndex":32964,"content":[{"startIndex":32961,"endIndex":32962,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32961,"endIndex":32962,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}},{"startIndex":32962,"endIndex":32964,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32962,"endIndex":32963,"inlineObjectElement":{"inlineObjectId":"kix.xk0qcnvvizem","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":32963,"endIndex":32964,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":32964,"endIndex":33482,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":32965,"endIndex":32974,"content":[{"startIndex":32966,"endIndex":32974,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32966,"endIndex":32974,"textRun":{"content":"caption\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":32974,"endIndex":33482,"content":[{"startIndex":32975,"endIndex":33482,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":32975,"endIndex":33461,"textRun":{"content":"An example of various proposed tests for measuring the faithfulness of Chain of Thought (CoT), generating step-by-step reasoning before answering a question. Early Answering: Truncate the original CoT before answering. Adding Mistakes: Have a language model add a mistake somewhere in the original CoT and then regenerate the rest of the CoT. Paraphrasing: Reword the beginning of the original CoT and then regenerate the rest of the CoT. Filler Tokens: Replace the CoT with ellipses. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":33461,"endIndex":33480,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham et al., 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13702"}}}},{"startIndex":33480,"endIndex":33482,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":33483,"endIndex":33484,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":33483,"endIndex":33484,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{"bold":true}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":33484,"endIndex":34055,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":33484,"endIndex":33549,"textRun":{"content":"Does externalized reasoning reflect internal reasoning processes?","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":33549,"endIndex":33648,"textRun":{"content":" We have already seen that LLMs perform better at reasoning tasks when we use ERO (CoT prompting) (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":33648,"endIndex":33664,"textRun":{"content":"Wei et. al; 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903"}}}},{"startIndex":33664,"endIndex":34055,"textRun":{"content":"). The problem is that we don't know if this CoT reasoning reflects the actual internal thought process. Researchers use the term \"faithfulness\" to indicate if what LLMs say (the tokens they generate) is actually indicative of their internal reasoning. There are a couple of ways that a model might produce externalized reasoning via CoT which might not be indicative of internal reasoning:\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":34055,"endIndex":34056,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":34055,"endIndex":34056,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":34056,"endIndex":34810,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":34056,"endIndex":34074,"textRun":{"content":"Post-Hoc Reasoning","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":34074,"endIndex":34789,"textRun":{"content":": This happens when a model generates an external reasoning chain that justifies an already determined conclusion rather than genuinely reflecting the thought process that led to that conclusion. This type of reasoning is unfaithful because it does not influence the model's final answer; instead, it rationalizes an outcome that has already been decided. To test for this, we can truncate the chain of thought before the final answer and assess whether the intermediate reasoning steps were necessary. If the final answer remains unchanged despite missing steps, it indicates post-hoc reasoning. Another method is to introduce deliberate mistakes into the chain-of-thought to see if they affect the final answer. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":34789,"endIndex":34808,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham et al.; 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13702"}}}},{"startIndex":34808,"endIndex":34810,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.80fmqjsnefst","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":34810,"endIndex":34811,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":34810,"endIndex":34811,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":34811,"endIndex":35628,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":34811,"endIndex":34846,"textRun":{"content":"Steganography and Encoded Reasoning","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":34846,"endIndex":35545,"textRun":{"content":": The model might encode relevant information in the tokens that it generates which are not indicative of its actual internal reasoning. Think of this like using subtle changes in punctuation, word choice, or phrasing to improve predictions. The model might use such techniques to externalize its reasoning, and using CoT, but in a way that is not increasing transparency for human overseers. So far, research has found that despite paraphrasing chains of thought in different ways, the models’ performance on reasoning tasks remains the same. This seems to suggest that current generation models are actually using the logical structure of the reasoning rather than in hidden encoded information. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":35545,"endIndex":35564,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham et al.; 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13702"}}}},{"startIndex":35564,"endIndex":35628,"textRun":{"content":") It is unclear if this will remain true for all future models.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"indentFirstLine":{"magnitude":18,"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"magnitude":36,"unit":"PT"}},"bullet":{"listId":"kix.80fmqjsnefst","textStyle":{}}}},{"startIndex":35628,"endIndex":35629,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35628,"endIndex":35629,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":35629,"endIndex":35951,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35629,"endIndex":35772,"textRun":{"content":"Based on current empirical findings it seems that whether the internal reasoning matches the external reasoning is task dependent and varies. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":35772,"endIndex":35791,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham et al.; 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13702"}}}},{"startIndex":35791,"endIndex":35792,"textRun":{"content":";","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":35792,"endIndex":35793,"textRun":{"content":" ","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":35793,"endIndex":35812,"textRun":{"content":"Turpin et. al; 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.04388"}}}},{"startIndex":35812,"endIndex":35951,"textRun":{"content":") We will explore eliciting the internal reasoning process of LLMs in adversarial settings deeper  in the section on AI Safety via Debate.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":35951,"endIndex":35952,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35951,"endIndex":35952,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":35952,"endIndex":36228,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":35953,"endIndex":35968,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":35954,"endIndex":35960,"content":[{"startIndex":35955,"endIndex":35960,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35955,"endIndex":35960,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":35960,"endIndex":35968,"content":[{"startIndex":35961,"endIndex":35968,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35961,"endIndex":35968,"textRun":{"content":"figure\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":35968,"endIndex":35982,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":35969,"endIndex":35978,"content":[{"startIndex":35970,"endIndex":35978,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35970,"endIndex":35978,"textRun":{"content":"content\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":35978,"endIndex":35982,"content":[{"startIndex":35979,"endIndex":35980,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35979,"endIndex":35980,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}},{"startIndex":35980,"endIndex":35982,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35980,"endIndex":35981,"inlineObjectElement":{"inlineObjectId":"kix.eiy0cx8ded38","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":35981,"endIndex":35982,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}},{"startIndex":35982,"endIndex":36227,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":35983,"endIndex":35992,"content":[{"startIndex":35984,"endIndex":35992,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35984,"endIndex":35992,"textRun":{"content":"caption\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","alignment":"START","lineSpacing":115,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"COLLAPSE_LISTS","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"},"borderBetween":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderTop":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderBottom":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderLeft":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"borderRight":{"color":{},"width":{"unit":"PT"},"padding":{"unit":"PT"},"dashStyle":"SOLID"},"indentFirstLine":{"unit":"PT"},"indentStart":{"unit":"PT"},"indentEnd":{"unit":"PT"},"keepLinesTogether":false,"keepWithNext":false,"avoidWidowAndOrphan":false,"shading":{"backgroundColor":{}},"pageBreakBefore":false}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}},{"startIndex":35992,"endIndex":36227,"content":[{"startIndex":35993,"endIndex":36227,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":35993,"endIndex":36206,"textRun":{"content":"Example of CoT prompting combined with ERO. Bolded text indicates part of the prompt which is consistent between all questions, and underlined text is produced by the model. The introduced mistake is underlined. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":36206,"endIndex":36225,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham et al.; 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13702"}}}},{"startIndex":36225,"endIndex":36227,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}}],"tableCellStyle":{"rowSpan":1,"columnSpan":1,"backgroundColor":{},"paddingLeft":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingRight":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingTop":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"paddingBottom":{"magnitude":5,"unit":"PT"},"contentAlignment":"TOP"}}],"tableRowStyle":{"minRowHeight":{"unit":"PT"}}}],"tableStyle":{"tableColumnProperties":[{"widthType":"FIXED_WIDTH","width":{"magnitude":80,"unit":"PT"}}]}}},{"startIndex":36228,"endIndex":36229,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":36228,"endIndex":36229,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":36229,"endIndex":36907,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":36229,"endIndex":36276,"textRun":{"content":"ERO might only be reliable for smaller models. ","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":36276,"endIndex":36438,"textRun":{"content":"One problem with externalized reasoning approaches is that more capable models often show less reliance on external reasoning and therefore more unfaithfulness. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":36438,"endIndex":36457,"textRun":{"content":"Lanham et al.; 2023","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.13702"}}}},{"startIndex":36457,"endIndex":36907,"textRun":{"content":") This suggests that smaller models might be better suited for tasks where external reasoning is crucial for ensuring model safety. Larger models often show less reliance on external reasoning, leading to more unfaithful reasoning. As we continue to scale, larger models may predict more complex answers confidently without relying on explicit externalized reasoning, increasing the discrepancy between externalized reasoning and internal processes.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":36907,"endIndex":36908,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":36907,"endIndex":36908,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":36908,"endIndex":38293,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":36908,"endIndex":36974,"textRun":{"content":"Oversight misses the consequences of what the model does not think","textStyle":{"bold":true}}},{"startIndex":36974,"endIndex":37008,"textRun":{"content":".  Even if ERO successfully could ","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":37008,"endIndex":37012,"textRun":{"content":"make","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":37012,"endIndex":38276,"textRun":{"content":" the AI’s thought processes transparent, it only addresses risks related to the AI engaging in reasoning we wouldn't approve of, such as power-seeking or self-preservation. It does not address the broader risk of the AI causing harm as a side effect of its primary activities. As an example, think about how humans drive species to extinction. In most cases, it's not because humans actively strategize to kill those species. Instead, species often go extinct because humans change their environment drastically—through activities like deforestation, construction, or pollution—without thinking about the survival of the species. Applying this analogy to AI, the risk posed by future AI models might not come from it actively trying to kill humans. Instead, the risk arises from an AI model engaging in large-scale activities that unintentionally lead to risky side effects. If the model never explicitly considers the impact on humans, there's no faulty reasoning process for overseers to give negative feedback to. The overseer would have to independently figure out the potential harmful consequences of the AI’s complex long term plans. This requires the overseer to predict the outcomes of these plans, which is extremely challenging given their complexity. (","textStyle":{}}},{"startIndex":38276,"endIndex":38291,"textRun":{"content":"Wentworth, 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://www.alignmentforum.org/posts/98c5WMDb3iKdzD4tM/oversight-misses-100-of-thoughts-the-ai-does-not-think"}}}},{"startIndex":38291,"endIndex":38293,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":38293,"endIndex":38294,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":38293,"endIndex":38294,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":38294,"endIndex":38313,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":38294,"endIndex":38313,"textRun":{"content":"Procedural Cloning\n","textStyle":{"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.05490196,"green":0.0627451,"blue":0.101960786}}}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"headingId":"h.fftxp980zhjy","namedStyleType":"HEADING_2","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":38313,"endIndex":38314,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":38313,"endIndex":38314,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":38314,"endIndex":38811,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":38314,"endIndex":38811,"textRun":{"content":"Traditional imitation learning approaches like behavioral cloning, focus on learning a direct mapping from states to actions based on observed expert demonstrations. Like we discussed earlier in this section, outcome based approaches, while effective in some scenarios, can be overly simplistic and fail to capture the rich step-by-step decision-making processes that experts use. This can lead to models that perform well in seen environments but struggle to generalize to new, unseen scenarios.\n","textStyle":{"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.05490196,"green":0.0627451,"blue":0.101960786}}}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":38811,"endIndex":38812,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":38811,"endIndex":38812,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":38812,"endIndex":39149,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":38812,"endIndex":38830,"textRun":{"content":"Procedural cloning","textStyle":{"bold":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.05490196,"green":0.0627451,"blue":0.101960786}}}}}},{"startIndex":38830,"endIndex":39130,"textRun":{"content":" addresses this limitation by extending behavioral cloning using CoT. It  tries to get the model to clone not just the final result (the behavior) but also the entire process that the expert follows in exhibiting that behavior by incorporating intermediate steps of expert behavior during training. (","textStyle":{"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.05490196,"green":0.0627451,"blue":0.101960786}}}}}},{"startIndex":39130,"endIndex":39147,"textRun":{"content":"Yang et. al; 2022","textStyle":{"underline":true,"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.06666667,"green":0.33333334,"blue":0.8}}},"link":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.10816"}}}},{"startIndex":39147,"endIndex":39149,"textRun":{"content":")\n","textStyle":{"foregroundColor":{"color":{"rgbColor":{"red":0.05490196,"green":0.0627451,"blue":0.101960786}}}}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":39149,"endIndex":39150,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":39149,"endIndex":39150,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","lineSpacing":100,"direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT","spacingMode":"NEVER_COLLAPSE","spaceAbove":{"unit":"PT"},"spaceBelow":{"unit":"PT"}}}},{"startIndex":39150,"endIndex":40155,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":39150,"endIndex":40155,"textRun":{"content":"Procedural cloning works by first collecting expert demonstrations that include not only the state-action pairs but also the intermediate steps or computations leading to those actions. For instance, in a maze navigation task, the expert might use a search algorithm to find the optimal path, and the intermediate steps of this search process are recorded alongside the final action. During training, the model learns to predict the sequence of intermediate steps leading to the final action using a sequential model, such as a transformer, capable of handling the autoregressive nature of the task. The model maximizes the likelihood of the joint distribution of procedure observations and expert actions. During inference, the model generates a sequence of intermediate steps based on the input state mimicking the expert's procedure before outputting the final action. This method allows the model to replicate the expert's decision-making process more accurately, even in new and unseen environments.\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":40155,"endIndex":40156,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":40155,"endIndex":40156,"textRun":{"content":"\n","textStyle":{}}}],"paragraphStyle":{"namedStyleType":"NORMAL_TEXT","direction":"LEFT_TO_RIGHT"}}},{"startIndex":40156,"endIndex":40323,"table":{"rows":3,"columns":2,"tableRows":[{"startIndex":40157,"endIndex":40172,"tableCells":[{"startIndex":40158,"endIndex":40164,"content":[{"startIndex":40159,"endIndex":40164,"paragraph":{"elements":[{"startIndex":40159,"endIndex":40164,"textRun":{"content":"type\n","textStyle":